2026-03-02 01:44:08,318 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 01:44:10,505 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm feeling a bit down today, been missing my ex boyfriend and feeling a bit sad.
2026-03-02 01:44:11,201 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds hard to carry. Can you tell me more about what specifically makes you feel sad right now?
2026-03-02 01:44:14,857 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I broke up with him and now I miss him and want him back. I know I shouldn't have broken up but I do it anyway.
2026-03-02 01:44:15,214 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you're carrying some guilt about the breakup. What do you think you could have done differently in that situation?
2026-03-02 01:44:20,052 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I should have fought for him instead of letting him go. I also know he wasn't the best boyfriend but he was all I had and now I'm sad I let him go
2026-03-02 01:44:20,537 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s understandable to feel sad when you’ve invested so much in a relationship. What would it mean to you to make a choice that honors both your feelings and your growth?
2026-03-02 01:44:24,934 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I want to get him back because when I was with him I felt so important because everyone knew who he was in our small town and he was the most popular guy.
2026-03-02 01:44:25,387 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like your sense of self-worth was tied to being with him. What would it mean to you to build your confidence without relying on that connection?
2026-03-02 01:44:29,075 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It would be nice to not have to rely on a guy to feel important, I'm trying to focus on myself more.
2026-03-02 01:44:29,500 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and important step. How might you start small today to notice and celebrate something about yourself that doesn’t depend on someone else?
2026-03-02 01:44:33,630 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I can start by doing my makeup and hair nice and taking a nice selfie, something to make me feel pretty and nice today.
2026-03-02 01:44:34,201 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a gentle and meaningful start. Taking time to care for yourself like that can build confidence over time—especially when you do it with awareness and kindness. How did that feel when you did it?
2026-03-02 01:44:37,076 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It felt nice, I guess it made me feel a bit better to think about it more.
2026-03-02 01:44:37,639 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a great sign—small acts of self-care can gradually shift how you see yourself. Would you like to try one more thing together, like writing down one thing you appreciate about yourself today?
2026-03-02 01:44:39,667 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that would be nice, I can do that now.
2026-03-02 01:44:40,356 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Great. Take a moment to write down one thing you appreciate about yourself—something simple, like your kindness, your strength, or just how you’re showing up for yourself today. When you’re ready, I’m here to read it with you.
2026-03-02 01:44:42,541 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I appreciate that I am trying to make myself feel better today.
2026-03-02 01:44:43,111 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful and honest reflection. Recognizing your effort is a strong step toward self-compassion. Would you like to try something similar tomorrow—like noticing one small win in your day?
2026-03-02 01:44:45,935 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that would be great, it would be nice to keep the momentum going.
2026-03-02 01:44:46,435 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Perfect. You’re already building a stronger, more grounded sense of self. Let’s keep going—one small step at a time. How would you like to start tomorrow?
2026-03-02 01:44:49,653 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would like to notice one small win tomorrow, something that I accomplished during the day.
2026-03-02 01:44:50,385 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Great choice. A small win—like finishing a task, being patient, or just showing up—can build confidence over time. When you notice it, take a moment to say, “I did that. I’m proud of myself.” How does that feel?
2026-03-02 01:44:52,770 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It sounds nice, I can do that tomorrow. Thank you!
2026-03-02 01:44:53,371 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Thank you for being so open and honest. Remember, progress isn’t about perfection—it’s about showing up. I’m here if you’d like to talk more anytime. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:44:56,293 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you for your help today, I will take your suggestions and keep trying.
2026-03-02 01:44:56,326 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 01:44:56,890 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're absolutely welcome. It’s wonderful that you’re choosing to grow and care for yourself. Keep going—every small step counts. I’ll be here when you’re ready to talk again. 💙
2026-03-02 01:44:58,445 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you, have a nice day!
2026-03-02 01:44:58,478 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 01:44:58,981 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for being so open and kind. I’ll take that with me too. Have a peaceful and thoughtful day. I’ll be here whenever you need to talk. 💙
