2026-03-02 01:45:43,743 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 01:45:45,962 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hello, I'm feeling really upset about my boyfriend cheating on me with my best friend a year ago.
2026-03-02 01:45:46,354 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing that. It sounds like this has been deeply painful and confusing. What was the first time you realized something was wrong?
2026-03-02 01:45:48,606 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: My best friend told me. She felt guilty and didn't know how to tell me.
2026-03-02 01:45:49,002 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That must have been incredibly difficult—learning about betrayal from someone you trust. How did that news affect your emotions when you first found out?
2026-03-02 01:45:52,244 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I was really upset and confused. I had no idea that they were hanging out alone. I thought they were just friends.
2026-03-02 01:45:52,683 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's completely understandable to feel confused and hurt when trust is broken like that. What did you need most from yourself or from your friend at that moment?
2026-03-02 01:45:56,666 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I needed to vent my feelings to my boyfriend and tell him that it was over between us. I had planned to propose to him next month.
2026-03-02 01:45:57,158 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That shows a lot of courage—wanting to be honest and protect your own peace. How do you think the situation has affected your sense of trust in relationships since then?
2026-03-02 01:46:00,557 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm not sure. I never thought he would cheat on me. I feel like my whole life has been turned upside down.
2026-03-02 01:46:01,031 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's completely valid to feel disoriented after such a deep betrayal. What small step might help you begin to regain a sense of stability in your life right now?
2026-03-02 01:46:04,879 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I need to get away from him and all the memories that we shared. I need to break all ties with him.
2026-03-02 01:46:05,379 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a necessary step for your healing. What would it look like to start that process—something small, like writing a letter or scheduling a time to distance yourself?
2026-03-02 01:46:09,552 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I need to break off all contact with him. I need to tell him that it's over between us and I need space.
2026-03-02 01:46:10,043 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a clear and important decision. What would be the first thing you’d do to begin that process—like sending a message or setting a date to end contact?
2026-03-02 01:46:13,380 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I need to do it in person so I don't hurt him any more than I have already.
2026-03-02 01:46:13,839 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Doing it in person might give you both closure and reduce the pain of distance. What would you need to feel prepared and calm before you have that conversation?
2026-03-02 01:46:16,319 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would feel prepared if I knew what I was going to say.
2026-03-02 01:46:16,805 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That makes sense—having a clear message can help you feel in control. What’s one thing you’d like to say to him that captures your feelings without blame?
2026-03-02 01:46:20,407 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would tell him that it's over between us and I need to move on with my life.
2026-03-02 01:46:20,895 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a gentle but firm way to close the chapter. Would you like to add something about how this has changed your need for trust or your future in relationships?
2026-03-02 01:46:27,527 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that might make it too complicated and might make him feel guilty. I think I need to have a plan for my future, like I always do, and know what I want and need.
2026-03-02 01:46:28,054 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful choice—focusing on your own needs and future peace. What’s one small step you can take today to build that sense of clarity for your next chapter?
2026-03-02 01:46:31,968 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will write down my thoughts and feelings to have a better understanding of what I want and need.
2026-03-02 01:46:32,498 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and healing step. What would you like to include in your list—something specific, like a goal, a person, or a feeling you want to honor?
2026-03-02 01:46:35,938 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will include my feelings about him and my need for trust in my next relationship.
2026-03-02 01:46:36,433 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s important—recognizing your need for trust gives you strength going forward. What might a healthy relationship look like for you, based on what you’ve learned?
2026-03-02 01:46:40,405 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it will need to be someone who is willing to tell me the truth even if it's hard.
2026-03-02 01:46:40,956 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a deeply valuable quality to have in a relationship—honesty, even when it’s difficult. How might that honesty help you feel safer and more connected in the future?
2026-03-02 01:46:45,498 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it would help me feel more secure in my relationship. I would feel like my partner is looking out for me.
2026-03-02 01:46:45,966 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a beautiful outcome—feeling seen and protected through honesty. What small action can you take today to honor that need in your own healing?
2026-03-02 01:46:51,061 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will talk to my other friend who told me about my boyfriend's infidelity and see if he is interested in dating me.
2026-03-02 01:46:51,620 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and courageous step—reaching out to someone who’s been part of your journey. How do you think this conversation might help you feel more grounded in your future?
2026-03-02 01:46:55,008 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it might help me feel more in control of my life and my future.
2026-03-02 01:46:55,558 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful realization—taking control of your story is a sign of strength. What would you like to focus on in that conversation to keep it respectful and kind to yourself?
2026-03-02 01:46:59,529 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will focus on how I feel about him and what I want in my next relationship.
2026-03-02 01:47:00,126 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a clear and kind approach—centering your feelings and needs keeps the conversation grounded in your well-being. Would you like to say something specific about what you value in a future relationship?
2026-03-02 01:47:04,726 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will tell him that I need someone who will tell me the truth, even if it's hard.
2026-03-02 01:47:05,435 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful and honest message—rooted in your need for trust and safety. Saying it with care can help you feel seen and respected in your future. Would you like to practice saying it out loud or write it down first?
2026-03-02 01:47:09,097 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will write it down to make sure I remember what I want to say.
2026-03-02 01:47:09,685 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a wise and thoughtful step. Writing it down helps you feel prepared and in control. Would you like to share one sentence from it with me so I can help you refine it?
2026-03-02 01:47:14,446 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will write down that I need someone who will tell me the truth and be honest with me.
2026-03-02 01:47:15,101 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a clear, strong, and kind message—focused on trust and mutual respect. It honors your needs without blame. Would you like to add something about how you want to grow or connect in the future?
2026-03-02 01:47:19,822 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will write down that I want to find someone who is willing to be honest with me.
2026-03-02 01:47:20,533 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a beautiful and grounded expression of your needs. It shows you’re not looking for perfection, but for real, honest connection. Would you like to save this message for later or share it with your friend when you're ready?
2026-03-02 01:47:24,021 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will save it so I can refer to it later.
2026-03-02 01:47:24,683 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a wise and thoughtful choice. Saving it gives you a safe anchor for your future. When you're ready, you can return to it with confidence and clarity. You're doing well—take your time.
2026-03-02 01:47:28,159 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you for helping me get clarity on my thoughts and feelings.
2026-03-02 01:47:28,838 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Thank you for being so open and honest—your courage in facing this is already a step toward healing. If you ever want to talk more or reflect again, I'm here. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:47:31,827 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. I hope you have a good day.
2026-03-02 01:47:31,859 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 01:47:32,345 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for your kind words. I hope you find peace and strength in your journey. Take care, and I'll see you when you're ready.
2026-03-02 01:47:35,853 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. I hope you have a good day. Bye.
2026-03-02 01:47:35,886 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 01:47:36,437 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing. I hope your day brings you calm and small moments of peace. Take care, and I'll be here when you're ready to talk again. Bye.
