2026-03-02 01:51:14,180 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 01:51:17,808 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm feeling pretty good today. Not too much is going on. I think it's good to be able to talk to you again.
2026-03-02 01:51:18,165 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds nice—appreciate you reaching out. What’s one small thing that’s been helping you feel good lately?
2026-03-02 01:51:21,865 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Well, I was thinking about dropping one of my classes. It's not too late yet. I'm not sure if I should do that.
2026-03-02 01:51:22,351 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful decision. What makes you think dropping that class might be a good move? Is it something you're worried about, or something you're actually excited about?
2026-03-02 01:51:25,636 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm worried that I won't be able to keep up. The semester just started and I'm feeling a bit overwhelmed.
2026-03-02 01:51:26,139 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It makes sense to feel overwhelmed at the start of a new semester. What would it look like if you dropped that class—how might that change your daily routine or stress levels?
2026-03-02 01:51:28,579 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would have more free time. Not have to worry about a fourth class.
2026-03-02 01:51:29,073 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a real benefit—more time and less pressure. How might that extra time feel when you actually use it, like for rest, hobbies, or planning something new?
2026-03-02 01:51:32,255 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I might go for a run more often. I'm worried that I won't use the time effectively.
2026-03-02 01:51:32,842 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a great goal—running can be both energizing and grounding. What would it look like to start with just one run a week, and how might that small step feel different from the current schedule?
2026-03-02 01:51:35,759 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would feel a bit better. Like I was doing something to help my situation.
2026-03-02 01:51:36,236 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s powerful—feeling like you’re taking an active step can really shift your mindset. What would you say to yourself if you successfully did that one run?
2026-03-02 01:51:39,545 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm doing better than I was before. I'm not letting the stress get to me as much.
2026-03-02 01:51:39,903 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a meaningful shift. How might that sense of progress feel when you reflect on it in a few days?
2026-03-02 01:51:42,736 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it would be nice to know that I was able to do something productive.
2026-03-02 01:51:43,282 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and healthy goal—feeling productive, even in small ways, can build confidence. What would you like to try next, if you had one small step to take?
2026-03-02 01:51:46,922 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I'll see how I do for a while. I'll talk to my boss about more hours.
2026-03-02 01:51:47,297 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a thoughtful and realistic next step. What would you hope to feel or achieve if that conversation went well?
2026-03-02 01:51:50,193 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would feel less financial stress. I would feel like I'm in control.
2026-03-02 01:51:50,757 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful motivation—feeling in control can make a big difference. What would a small success in that conversation look like, even if it’s just a small change in your schedule?
2026-03-02 01:51:53,659 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would have more hours. I could use that money to pay some bills.
2026-03-02 01:51:54,138 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a clear and practical goal. What might it feel like when you actually start using those extra hours to pay off a bill you’ve been worrying about?
2026-03-02 01:51:57,431 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would feel relieved. I would feel more confident in my ability to manage my finances.
2026-03-02 01:51:57,963 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong sense of progress—confidence grows when you take small, intentional steps. What would you say to yourself when you look back on this moment in a few weeks?
2026-03-02 01:52:01,446 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm doing a better job than before. I'm not feeling as overwhelmed as I was.
2026-03-02 01:52:01,980 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a meaningful shift—your ability to stay grounded and keep moving forward is a real strength. How might you want to build on that sense of progress in the coming week?
2026-03-02 01:52:05,162 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I'll just keep going. Keep doing the things that I'm doing.
2026-03-02 01:52:05,776 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a wise and sustainable approach. By staying consistent with what works, you’re building confidence and stability. How would you like to check in with yourself in a few days to see how you’re doing?
2026-03-02 01:52:09,327 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I'll talk to you again in a few days. See how things are going.
2026-03-02 01:52:09,894 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a great plan. I’ll be here whenever you’re ready to talk. How would you like to start checking in—maybe with a simple question or just a quick update?
2026-03-02 01:52:12,935 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I'll just talk to you again. Thanks for your help.
2026-03-02 01:52:12,967 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 01:52:13,528 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Remember, you don’t have to have all the answers—just showing up and being honest is already a strength. When you're ready, I'm here. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:52:15,244 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: You too. Thanks again. Bye.
