2026-03-02 01:56:29,705 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 01:56:33,121 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hi, I'm sad and lonely. I broke up with my boyfriend and now I want him back, but he doesn't care about me.
2026-03-02 01:56:33,677 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing that. It sounds like you're feeling hurt and longing for connection after the breakup. What would it mean to you to have him back—what do you hope to regain through that?
2026-03-02 01:56:36,173 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I want to feel important again. We were popular in my small town and I liked it.
2026-03-02 01:56:36,750 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you value being seen and appreciated, especially in a community where your presence mattered. What would it look like if you felt important again—not just through him, but through your own life or relationships?
2026-03-02 01:56:39,278 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I could feel important through school or friendships, but I think I still need him.
2026-03-02 01:56:39,922 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That's a valid feeling—desire for connection can be deeply meaningful. What would it look like if you reached out to someone new or reconnected with a friend, even just a little, and noticed how it made you feel?
2026-03-02 01:56:43,072 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I briefly liked someone else and broke up with him. Now I see him with other girls and it makes me jealous.
2026-03-02 01:56:43,574 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you're carrying a strong emotional investment in being loved and seen. How do you think your feelings of jealousy connect to the need for being important in your relationships?
2026-03-02 01:56:47,317 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I'm scared that someone else will get him before I can, so I need to hurry and get him back.
2026-03-02 01:56:47,946 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That fear—of losing him before you can—makes sense and shows how much you value his presence. What might happen if you paused and noticed what you actually want from a relationship, instead of just what you fear losing?
2026-03-02 01:56:53,008 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I want him back because he's the only guy that has ever made me feel special and loved. I think I got spoiled by it and now I want it again.
2026-03-02 01:56:53,579 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you’re deeply attached to the feeling of being loved and special. What would it mean to you to feel loved in a way that doesn’t depend on someone else’s actions or attention?
2026-03-02 01:56:56,646 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm not sure what it would be like. Maybe I'm just not cut out for happiness.
2026-03-02 01:56:57,393 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s okay to not know yet—many people feel that way when they’re navigating deep emotions. What small step might you take today to notice what kind of love or connection feels safe and real to you, even if it’s different from what you’ve known before?
2026-03-02 01:57:01,325 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I need to talk to him again. I'm going to text him and see if he wants to talk.
2026-03-02 01:57:01,882 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a brave and thoughtful step. How might you check in with yourself before or after the text—like noticing your feelings or what you hope to learn—without expecting a specific outcome?
2026-03-02 01:57:07,612 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will try to remain calm and not overthink it too much. I want to let him know that I'm sorry for breaking up and if he wants to try again.
2026-03-02 01:57:08,271 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a kind and balanced approach. What might you notice if you pause for a moment before sending the message—like your breath, your heart rate, or your words—so you’re not reacting out of fear or pressure?
2026-03-02 01:57:11,677 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'll take some deep breaths and think about what I'm feeling before sending the message.
2026-03-02 01:57:12,265 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful self-compassionate practice. What might you notice if you pause after you send the message—without waiting for a reply—and simply observe how you feel in your body or mind?
2026-03-02 01:57:17,805 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I'll feel a mix of emotions and maybe a little scared. I'll try to stay positive and hopeful that he will want to try again.
2026-03-02 01:57:18,556 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s completely normal to feel a mix of emotions—hope, fear, even uncertainty. What might it mean if, even if he doesn’t respond or changes his mind, you still honor your own worth and the effort you’ve made to care for your feelings?
2026-03-02 01:57:22,040 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would be able to feel better about myself and know that I tried my best.
2026-03-02 01:57:22,662 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful realization. Trying your best, even when the outcome is uncertain, shows strength and self-respect. How might you gently remind yourself of that when you feel down or uncertain in the future?
2026-03-02 01:57:26,021 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I could try to write down positive affirmations to help remind me of my self worth.
2026-03-02 01:57:26,711 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and kind practice. What might your affirmations look like—something simple, like “I am worthy of love and care, even if it doesn’t come from him”? Try one today and see how it feels.
2026-03-02 01:57:29,541 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will definitely try that today. Thank you for your help and guidance.
2026-03-02 01:57:30,274 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It’s meaningful that you’re taking these small, thoughtful steps—each one builds your self-awareness and peace. If you ever want to talk more or reflect on how you’re feeling, I’m here. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:57:32,358 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thanks again. I'll talk to you soon.
2026-03-02 01:57:32,391 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 01:57:32,829 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Absolutely—feel free to reach out whenever you’re ready. Wishing you calm, clarity, and kindness as you move forward. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:57:34,167 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: You too. Thanks again.
2026-03-02 01:57:34,200 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 01:57:34,776 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. I'm glad I could support you. Take care, and remember—you're doing your best, and that matters. I'll be here when you're ready to talk again.
