2026-03-02 01:58:46,708 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 01:58:50,467 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hello! I am so glad you are here to listen to me. I am very upset. I just found out my boyfriend cheated on me with my best friend a year ago.
2026-03-02 01:58:51,061 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing that with me. That sounds incredibly painful—being betrayed by someone you trusted so deeply must feel devastating. What’s one thing that comes to mind when you think about how you’re feeling right now?
2026-03-02 01:58:53,919 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Everything is wrong. I thought everything was going so well and now I just don’t know what to do.
2026-03-02 01:58:54,398 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s completely understandable to feel lost after such a deep betrayal. What’s one small thing you’ve noticed yourself doing or feeling when you’re in this moment of confusion?
2026-03-02 01:58:59,072 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I have been thinking about another man that has shown interest in me for about a year now but I never thought of him as a possibility because I was so happy with my boyfriend.
2026-03-02 01:58:59,585 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a significant shift in your thoughts—and it’s okay to notice it. How does that idea of him making you feel, even just slightly, when you think about it?
2026-03-02 01:59:03,048 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It makes me feel like I might have wasted a year of my life with the wrong person and I should consider this other option.
2026-03-02 01:59:03,629 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you’re carrying a lot of regret and a strong sense of what might have been. What would a small step look like if you wanted to explore that possibility without making a decision right now?
2026-03-02 01:59:07,216 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I’m not sure. I would have to see if he is interested still and how to move forward in that aspect.
2026-03-02 01:59:07,759 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That makes sense—taking things slowly can help protect your emotional well-being. What would it look like if you reached out to him with just one gentle question, to see where he stands?
2026-03-02 01:59:11,354 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I can do that. I just need to decide if I want to keep my relationship with my boyfriend or end it.
2026-03-02 01:59:11,863 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful and important decision. What would one small step look like if you wanted to explore your feelings about staying with your boyfriend—without making a final choice yet?
2026-03-02 01:59:15,069 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I can talk with him more and ask him if he still wants to get engaged and married as planned.
2026-03-02 01:59:15,631 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and respectful way to approach it. How do you think he might respond if he says yes, or if he says no? What would that mean for you in that moment?
2026-03-02 01:59:21,761 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: If he says yes, it will give me more confidence to stay with him. If he says no, I think it would mean that he isn’t serious about our relationship and I should end it.
2026-03-02 01:59:22,326 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you’re using his answer as a guide, which is valid. What would happen in your body or mind if you decided to end the relationship—before you even say the words?
2026-03-02 01:59:26,742 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would feel relieved. I would be so angry and upset but also feel like I am taking back control of my life.
2026-03-02 01:59:27,286 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful insight—feeling relief and reclaiming control are important parts of healing. What might you do in the next few days to honor that feeling without rushing into action?
2026-03-02 01:59:33,567 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will talk with my boyfriend about the possibility of ending our relationship and see what he thinks. I will also reach out to the other man to see if he is still interested.
2026-03-02 01:59:34,077 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a balanced and thoughtful path forward. How do you think you’ll feel when you’re actually having that conversation with your boyfriend—before you make any decisions?
2026-03-02 01:59:38,704 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will be anxious and scared about what he will say but I know I need to hear it to make a decision.
2026-03-02 01:59:39,273 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s completely normal to feel anxious when facing something so important. What might you say to yourself before the conversation to remind yourself that you’re doing this for your own peace and well-being?
2026-03-02 01:59:43,953 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I can say that I am doing this for me and my future and I deserve someone who is honest and serious about our relationship.
2026-03-02 01:59:44,593 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful and compassionate affirmation. Saying it to yourself can help ground you in your values when the emotions come up. Would you like to try saying it aloud in a quiet moment, just to feel it again?
2026-03-02 01:59:47,910 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would like that. Thank you so much for your help. I really appreciate it!
2026-03-02 01:59:48,584 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You’re very welcome. It’s okay to take your time and honor your feelings. If you’d like to check in again later—or just want to talk more—feel free to reach out. You’re not alone in this.
2026-03-02 01:59:51,062 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. I hope you have a wonderful day! Bye.
2026-03-02 01:59:51,095 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 01:59:51,604 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing your journey with me. Wishing you peace, clarity, and strength as you move forward. If anything comes up, I’m here. Take care.
2026-03-02 01:59:52,669 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you! Bye.
2026-03-02 01:59:52,702 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 01:59:53,187 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Wishing you calm and courage in whatever comes next. Take care, and I’ll be here if you need to talk again. Bye.
