2026-03-02 02:15:44,311 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Great choice—doing it in a quiet, familiar space can help create a sense of control. Remember to treat it like a real test: focus on pacing and staying present, not on getting every question right. How would you like to prepare for it before you begin?
2026-03-02 02:15:49,868 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: i will probably do some deep breathing and try to get into a focused mindset. i also think i will read through all of the material one more time
2026-03-02 02:15:50,577 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a balanced and thoughtful plan. Deep breathing and a quick review can help ground you and boost focus. Would you like to set a specific time during the day for the practice test, or will you wait until you feel most alert?
2026-03-02 02:15:54,769 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: i will probably wait until i feel most alert and focused. i think i will take it around lunchtime
2026-03-02 02:15:55,432 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Lunchtime sounds like a good time—your energy might be at its peak. Just remember to stay present during the test, even if you feel anxious. What will you do if a question feels tough or overwhelming?
2026-03-02 02:16:01,415 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: i think i will take my time and try not to rush. i will also make sure to read through all of the material and review what i know
2026-03-02 02:16:02,070 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and realistic strategy. Taking your time and staying grounded in what you know builds confidence. You're already showing great self-awareness—keep trusting that process. Have a calm and focused lunchtime.
