2026-03-02 02:16:09,359 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 02:16:12,820 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I am really upset, my boyfriend cheated on me with my best friend, I feel betrayed and everything in my life is wrong. I'm not sure what to do
2026-03-02 02:16:13,483 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: I'm sorry you're going through such a painful experience. It sounds like the betrayal has deeply shaken your sense of trust and safety. What would you like to explore first—how you're feeling right now, or what you're considering doing next?
2026-03-02 02:16:16,598 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm feeling like I should break up with him because he cheated and he still wants me to be engaged to him.
2026-03-02 02:16:17,195 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's completely valid to feel that breaking up is the right choice for you. What would it mean to you to end the relationship—emotionally, practically, or in terms of how you'd feel about yourself afterward?
2026-03-02 02:16:21,617 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will feel like I failed because I have had such strict plans for my life. I will feel bad about myself because I wasted so much time with the wrong person.
2026-03-02 02:16:22,306 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's important to recognize that your feelings of failure don't reflect your worth. You've been working hard on your life, and that effort matters. What if you saw your plans as something you can rebuild, rather than something you've failed to achieve?
2026-03-02 02:16:26,195 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: That sounds easy to say but I have a hard time rebuilding things, I tend to feel like I have to be in control by having strict plans.
2026-03-02 02:16:26,801 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's okay to feel stuck—control can feel like a way to protect yourself from pain. What would it look like if you allowed yourself to take small, uncertain steps instead of waiting for everything to be perfect?
2026-03-02 02:16:30,238 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would be out of control and that makes me very uncomfortable. I am more of a black and white person.
2026-03-02 02:16:30,918 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That makes sense—black and white thinking can offer clarity in times of chaos. What would it feel like to allow one small gray area, like just taking a step toward healing or talking to someone you trust, without needing everything to be perfect?
2026-03-02 02:16:33,386 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: That sounds nice but I still feel uncomfortable with it, I will try though.
2026-03-02 02:16:34,132 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and honest choice—trying, even when it’s uncomfortable, is a form of courage. How would you like to start, even if it’s just a small step, like writing one sentence about how you’re feeling or talking to someone you trust?
2026-03-02 02:16:37,055 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will talk to someone I trust about it. I already have someone in mind.
2026-03-02 02:16:37,730 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a meaningful and empowering step. Talking to someone you trust can help you feel seen and supported. What will you say when you talk to them—something you’ve been holding in, or a simple statement about how you’re feeling?
2026-03-02 02:16:41,033 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will tell them about my boyfriend cheating and how I feel like I should break up with him.
2026-03-02 02:16:41,515 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a brave and honest choice. Sharing your truth with someone you trust can be healing. What part of that conversation feels most difficult to say out loud?
2026-03-02 02:16:45,312 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think the part that is hard to say out loud is how I feel like I should break up with him.
2026-03-02 02:16:46,187 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s completely normal to feel that way—breaking up is a powerful decision that carries deep emotional weight. What if you said it not as a verdict, but as a question to yourself: “What does my heart need right now?” That might make it feel less like a failure and more like a step toward truth.
2026-03-02 02:16:48,574 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: That sounds nice, I will try to say it that way.
2026-03-02 02:16:49,320 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Great—taking that small shift in how you frame it can make all the difference. You’re already showing strength by choosing honesty and care over fear. Would you like to think about what you might say next, or would you prefer to focus on something else now?
2026-03-02 02:16:51,917 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would like to think about what I might say next.
2026-03-02 02:16:52,543 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: How about you start by writing one sentence that expresses your truth—like, “I’m feeling deeply hurt and I need to take time to understand what I want next.” Would that feel safe to say out loud?
2026-03-02 02:16:54,277 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: That would feel safe to say out loud.
2026-03-02 02:16:54,983 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful start. Saying it out loud, even just once, can help you feel seen and grounded. What if you read it aloud to yourself tomorrow, or share it with your trusted person—without pressure to decide anything right then?
2026-03-02 02:16:57,451 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will do that, read it aloud to myself.
2026-03-02 02:16:57,995 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a gentle and wise step. Reading it aloud gives your feelings space to be heard without judgment. How will you know when you're ready to share it with someone else?
2026-03-02 02:17:02,066 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will know when I am ready to share it with someone else when I feel comfortable with it.
2026-03-02 02:17:02,865 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a very healthy way to move forward—your comfort comes first. Trust that your readiness will grow with time, and you’re not alone in this journey. Would you like to check in again in a few days, or would you prefer to focus on something else now?
2026-03-02 02:17:05,718 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I would like to check in again in a few days.
2026-03-02 02:17:06,347 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and courageous choice. Taking time to reflect and process at your own pace is important. When you’re ready, we can continue talking—no pressure, just support. Take care of yourself.
2026-03-02 02:17:08,067 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. Have a nice day.
2026-03-02 02:17:08,100 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 02:17:08,538 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Remember, you're not alone in this. Take your time, and be kind to yourself. Have a peaceful day.
2026-03-02 02:17:10,277 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. Have a nice day.
2026-03-02 02:17:10,310 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 02:17:10,798 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Thank you for sharing your truth and taking such thoughtful steps. You're doing better than you think. Have a peaceful and restful day.
2026-03-02 02:17:10,798 - src.sim - INFO - Conversation ended.
