2026-03-02 02:17:13,105 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 02:17:17,050 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hey. Not so well. I was having feelings for a girl for a while. We started talking a month ago. I thought we might be more than friends in the future.
2026-03-02 02:17:17,395 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a meaningful connection. What happened recently that made you feel uncertain about the future of your relationship with her?
2026-03-02 02:17:20,132 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: She said she likes my friend. He's my closest friend. We've been friends for a decade.
2026-03-02 02:17:20,593 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That must be really hard to hear. How did you first find out about her liking your friend? Did it come as a surprise or was it something you expected?
2026-03-02 02:17:24,374 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It came as a surprise. I had feelings for her for a long time, so I wanted to see if anything would happen if we talked.
2026-03-02 02:17:24,829 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s natural to feel surprised when your hopes are challenged. How do you think her statement affects your sense of self-worth or your ability to move forward?
2026-03-02 02:17:28,866 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It made me sad and disappointed, but I'm trying to get over it. I feel like if she knew how I felt, she'd feel differently.
2026-03-02 02:17:29,373 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s okay to feel sad—your emotions are valid. What would it take for you to feel more at peace with this situation, even if she doesn’t change her feelings?
2026-03-02 02:17:32,528 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm trying to keep up my cheerful facade. I tell her that my friend is a good choice.
2026-03-02 02:17:32,956 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That shows a lot of strength in protecting your own well-being. What small step can you take today to honor both your feelings and your peace?
2026-03-02 02:17:38,697 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'll keep up what I'm doing. I don't know if it's right or wrong. I'm just trying to keep my head up and support my friend, even though it hurts.
2026-03-02 02:17:39,151 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're doing better than you think by staying grounded and kind. What would it mean to you if you could accept this situation without needing it to change?
2026-03-02 02:17:42,794 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would feel like I'm doing something wrong. Like maybe it's my fault she likes my friend instead of me.
2026-03-02 02:17:43,522 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s natural to feel that way, but it’s not your fault—her feelings are hers, and they don’t reflect your worth. What if you gently reframe it as a reminder that you’re still valuable, even when things don’t go as hoped?
2026-03-02 02:17:46,156 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'll try. I don't know how to tell them how sad I feel.
2026-03-02 02:17:46,840 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You don’t have to say anything if it feels uncomfortable. But if you ever want to share your sadness, even just with yourself, it can be a step toward healing. Would you like to try saying it out loud in a safe way?
2026-03-02 02:17:49,041 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'll try. Thanks for listening and helping me through this.
2026-03-02 02:17:49,561 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're welcome. Remember, it's okay to feel what you feel—even if it's hard. If you ever want to talk more, I'm here. Take care.
2026-03-02 02:17:50,354 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thanks. Bye.
2026-03-02 02:17:50,386 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 02:17:50,770 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're welcome. Take care, and remember you're not alone in this. If anything comes up, I'm here. Peace.
2026-03-02 02:17:51,966 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: You too. Thanks again.
2026-03-02 02:17:51,999 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
