2026-03-02 02:17:54,613 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 02:17:56,205 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hello, not feeling so good, just like the other days
2026-03-02 02:17:56,611 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: I notice you're saying you're not feeling well like other days. Is there something specific that's been on your mind or bothering you lately?
2026-03-02 02:18:02,029 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Well, I am just feeling unappreciated lately. I can't help but feel jealous when my cousin is out having fun in her new car, when I had to work so hard to get through college
2026-03-02 02:18:02,585 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you're carrying a deep sense of disappointment about not feeling appreciated compared to your cousin. What would it mean for you to feel valued in a way that matches the joy you see in her?
2026-03-02 02:18:08,889 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It's not just my cousin, my other cousins are also doing great and all the times I helped them out they never really appreciated me. I am just thinking that I will never be able to achieve what they have
2026-03-02 02:18:09,492 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you're carrying a sense of being overlooked, even when you've supported others. What would it take for you to believe that you *can* achieve something meaningful, even if it looks different from theirs?
2026-03-02 02:18:12,111 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I don't know. I feel like I am destined to live in poverty and struggle
2026-03-02 02:18:12,698 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That belief can feel very heavy. What would it look like if you started to see yourself as someone who is capable of building a better life, even if it takes time and steps you haven’t taken yet?
2026-03-02 02:18:16,652 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It is so hard. I can't even afford to buy myself a decent pair of shoes, let alone go on a holiday.
2026-03-02 02:18:17,245 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's hard to carry that weight when basic needs feel out of reach. What would a small step—something small and doable—look like if you started to build a sense of hope for the future?
2026-03-02 02:18:22,280 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I can start by counting every cent I have and not spending anything frivolous. I can also try to avoid investing until I can make more money
2026-03-02 02:18:22,778 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a very practical and thoughtful beginning. What would it feel like if you celebrated yourself for taking that first step—just showing up and being intentional with your money?
2026-03-02 02:18:27,183 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it will feel nice, but it is so hard to feel like I am doing well when my school work is so hard
2026-03-02 02:18:27,717 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s completely valid to feel overwhelmed when school is demanding. What would it look like if you allowed yourself to rest just a little—without guilt—while still working toward your goals?
2026-03-02 02:18:31,810 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I will have to work harder to get better at my studies so that I can have more time to rest
2026-03-02 02:18:32,297 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and realistic plan. What would a small, manageable part of that look like today—something you could do without feeling like it’s too much?
2026-03-02 02:18:35,404 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will have to just finish my work and not worry about it until tomorrow
2026-03-02 02:18:35,969 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a wise and kind choice—giving yourself space to manage without burning out. How do you think you’ll feel when you’ve finished today’s work and can finally take a breath?
2026-03-02 02:18:39,441 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will feel more at ease. Thanks for your help today. Have a nice day. Bye
2026-03-02 02:18:40,093 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: I'm glad we could walk through this together. Remember, you’re not alone in the journey—small steps like this build strength over time. If you'd like to check in again later, I'm here. Take care.
2026-03-02 02:18:43,439 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will keep that in mind. I hope you have a nice day as well. Bye
2026-03-02 02:18:43,472 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 02:18:43,960 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for being honest and open. You're doing better than you think, one small step at a time. I’ll see you when you’re ready. Take care.
2026-03-02 02:18:47,500 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will need to talk to you again when I get home. Bye for now.
2026-03-02 02:18:47,533 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 02:18:48,047 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a great plan. Talking when you’re ready will help you stay grounded. I’m here for you whenever you need to check in. Take care, and see you soon.
