2026-03-02 02:33:37,930 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 02:33:41,733 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm feeling down again. I guess I am just feeling like I am not appreciated for all the help I gave to my family in the past.
2026-03-02 02:33:42,448 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing that. It sounds like you’ve been giving a lot of love and support to your family, and it’s understandable to feel overlooked or unappreciated. What might be one specific moment or situation where you felt that your help wasn’t acknowledged?
2026-03-02 02:33:48,603 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: My cousin graduated college a few years ago. She is making a pretty good living now. I always babysat her when her parents were at work and I always helped her out when she needed money for school.
2026-03-02 02:33:49,084 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you went above and beyond to support her during important times. What might be one thing you wish she had said or done to show you appreciated your efforts?
2026-03-02 02:33:52,828 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I wish she had said thank you or at least something positive when she sees me. Instead I just get jealous and sad.
2026-03-02 02:33:53,664 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a really important insight — feeling unseen can deeply affect how we see our own worth. What might happen if you gently reminded yourself that your care was meaningful, even if it wasn’t expressed in words? Could you try noticing one small moment when you feel your value — even without her saying thank you?
2026-03-02 02:33:57,898 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I will try to focus on the good things that are happening in my life and try to not focus on my cousin's success.
2026-03-02 02:33:58,569 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and kind shift. What might one small, positive thing from your day feel like — something simple, like a kind word from a friend or a moment of calm? Trying to notice it could help recenter your focus.
2026-03-02 02:34:02,968 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I will try that and also try to spend more time with friends. I haven't been as social lately as I used to be.
2026-03-02 02:34:03,667 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong step — reconnecting with friends can bring warmth and balance. What might one small interaction with a friend feel like — just a text, a coffee, or a shared activity? Trying that could help ease the loneliness you're feeling.
2026-03-02 02:34:06,039 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you for your advice. I think I will try that tomorrow.
2026-03-02 02:34:06,628 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It's powerful that you're taking small, intentional steps. How would you like to check in with yourself tomorrow — maybe after spending time with a friend or noticing one positive moment?
2026-03-02 02:34:10,560 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would like to try to study a little bit less tomorrow so I can spend more time with my friends.
2026-03-02 02:34:11,191 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a balanced and kind choice — reducing study time to prioritize connection is a positive shift. What might one simple way be to gently reduce your study time, like setting a timer or choosing one topic to finish first?
2026-03-02 02:34:14,455 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you for your help. Have a good night. I will try your advice tomorrow.
2026-03-02 02:34:15,057 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It’s comforting to hear you’re taking care of yourself. How would you like to check in with yourself tomorrow — maybe by noticing one small moment of joy or connection with a friend?
2026-03-02 02:34:18,707 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I would like to check in tomorrow to see if I felt a little less jealous of my cousin.
2026-03-02 02:34:19,425 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and gentle way to track your progress. What might you notice — even a small shift — like a moment when you felt proud of yourself or a brief sense of peace instead of comparison? Checking in with that curiosity can be very helpful.
2026-03-02 02:34:22,952 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that will be very helpful. Thank you for your help. Have a good night.
2026-03-02 02:34:23,591 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It's meaningful that you're being kind to yourself and taking small steps. Sleep well, and remember — you don’t have to have all the answers. Just showing up with awareness is enough.
2026-03-02 02:34:26,428 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you for your help. I feel much better now. Goodbye.
2026-03-02 02:34:26,461 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 02:34:27,068 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. I'm glad I could support you. Remember, you're not alone in this journey — small shifts like these build strength over time. Take care, and see you again when you're ready.
2026-03-02 02:34:29,530 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Goodbye. Thank you again. Have a good night.
2026-03-02 02:34:29,563 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 02:34:30,025 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It's been a pleasure supporting you. Take care, and may each day bring you a little more peace and connection. Goodnight.
