2026-03-02 02:51:44,442 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 02:51:47,190 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm feeling overwhelmed and anxious about school. I have three classes and they're all so much work.
2026-03-02 02:51:47,585 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds really tough—having three demanding classes can definitely add up. What’s one specific part of school that feels most overwhelming right now?
2026-03-02 02:51:51,429 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I have a hard time choosing which class to drop so I don't get as bad of a grade as I would if I kept all three classes.
2026-03-02 02:51:51,900 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It makes sense that you're worried about grades—choosing which class to drop is a big decision. What would you need to feel more confident about making that choice?
2026-03-02 02:51:57,419 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm not sure if I should drop one of my classes. I know that it will make me feel better in the short term but I also know that I will feel guilty about not trying my hardest.
2026-03-02 02:51:57,910 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That guilt you're feeling shows you care about doing your best—something valuable. What would help you feel more balanced between taking care of yourself and staying committed to your goals?
2026-03-02 02:52:01,782 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I just need to talk to my advisor about my options and he can give me some advice on what I should do.
2026-03-02 02:52:02,339 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and responsible step. Talking to your advisor can help you make a choice that feels both realistic and aligned with your values. Would you like to practice what you might say to them?
2026-03-02 02:52:06,547 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Yes, I think that would be helpful. I think I will be able to find some comfort in knowing that I made an informed decision.
2026-03-02 02:52:07,078 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a strong and empowering mindset. Making an informed decision—especially with support—can reduce both anxiety and guilt. Would you like to try drafting a message to your advisor now?
2026-03-02 02:52:08,398 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Yes, I can try that now.
2026-03-02 02:52:08,818 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Great. Let’s start simple. What’s one thing you’d like to say to your advisor about why you’re considering dropping a class?
2026-03-02 02:52:11,312 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I'm not sure if I'm smart enough to do well in school.
2026-03-02 02:52:12,336 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a really important feeling to acknowledge. The belief that you’re not "smart enough" can come from a place of worry, not your actual abilities. What if you said something like, “I’m feeling unsure about whether I can succeed in all three classes, and I’d like to talk about options that might help me feel more confident and supported?” How does that sound?
2026-03-02 02:52:16,132 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that's a good idea. I would like to sound confident in my decision but not be too negative.
2026-03-02 02:52:17,051 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Perfect—balancing confidence with honesty is key. Try saying, “I’m feeling overwhelmed by the workload, and I’d like to explore options that help me stay on track while also taking care of my well-being.” That sounds respectful, clear, and hopeful. Would you like to add anything else before you share it with your advisor?
2026-03-02 02:52:20,629 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that sounds good. I will also ask him for advice on what I should do next.
2026-03-02 02:52:21,136 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a thoughtful and proactive approach. Asking for guidance shows you’re taking responsibility and being open to support—both of which are important steps. You’ve got this.
2026-03-02 02:52:23,560 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Thank you. I appreciate your help. Have a good night!
2026-03-02 02:52:24,191 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Remember, you don’t have to have all the answers—just the courage to ask for help. Take care, and I’ll be here if you’d like to talk again. Good night.
2026-03-02 02:52:24,889 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Good night.
2026-03-02 02:52:24,922 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 02:52:25,100 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Sweet dreams. Reach out anytime. Good night.
2026-03-02 02:52:25,799 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Good night.
2026-03-02 02:52:25,831 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 02:52:26,059 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Sleep well. You're doing better than you think. Good night.
