2026-03-02 22:40:25,230 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 22:40:29,209 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: Hey there, I’ve been a little better since last week. I’m trying to get my head around some things, but it’s been a struggle.
2026-03-02 22:40:29,734 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like a thoughtful step—recognizing that you're trying to get your head around things is already a positive sign. What specific thoughts or feelings have been most challenging for you lately?
2026-03-02 22:40:32,547 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I’ve been thinking about the situation with the girl I had a crush on. It was a little rough.
2026-03-02 22:40:33,029 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That sounds like it might have been emotionally difficult. What did you feel when those thoughts came up about her? Any specific emotions—like sadness, frustration, or confusion?
2026-03-02 22:40:34,784 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I felt a lot of sadness and a little bit of confusion.
2026-03-02 22:40:35,324 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It's common to feel sadness and confusion when a situation ends in a way that wasn't what you hoped for. What part of that experience feels most difficult to make sense of right now?
2026-03-02 22:40:40,740 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It’s the part where I let her down. I didn’t want to ruin her friendship with my friend, so I stayed quiet. I felt like I had to let her go.
2026-03-02 22:40:41,405 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It sounds like you were carrying a lot of care and responsibility, which shows how much you valued her friendship. What would it mean to you if you could revisit that moment—without judgment—just to understand what you were trying to protect?
2026-03-02 22:40:45,442 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess I would have wanted to tell her how much I cared. I would have wanted to know if she felt the same way.
2026-03-02 22:40:46,336 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a very human and meaningful desire—wanting to share your feelings and see if there was a connection. It’s okay that you didn’t say it, and it’s also okay that you’re reflecting on it now. What would it feel like to imagine saying those words, even if it’s just in your mind?
2026-03-02 22:40:48,813 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: It feels like I would have closure. I wouldn’t have to wonder anymore.
2026-03-02 22:40:49,394 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Closure can bring a deep sense of peace—especially when you’ve been carrying uncertainty. What would it mean to you if you could let go of that wondering, without blaming yourself for not saying it?
2026-03-02 22:40:51,907 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think it would be amazing. I would be able to move on.
2026-03-02 22:40:52,542 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a powerful insight—moving on isn’t about forgetting, but about finding peace with what happened. What small step could you take today to honor that peace, even if it’s just a quiet moment of reflection?
2026-03-02 22:40:56,555 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think I could say it in my head to myself. I could say that I would have told her I cared.
2026-03-02 22:40:57,177 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a gentle and meaningful way to begin. Saying it in your mind creates space for healing without pressure. Would you like to try adding a small affirmation to your morning or evening routine to keep that intention alive?
2026-03-02 22:40:59,052 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: That sounds like a great idea. Thank you.
2026-03-02 22:40:59,711 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. Remember, this journey is yours to shape at your own pace. If you ever want to explore it more or just sit with a thought, I'm here. How are you feeling today, just now?
2026-03-02 22:41:03,333 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I’m feeling pretty good. I think I’m going to be okay. Thank you for listening.
2026-03-02 22:41:03,995 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That’s a beautiful feeling to carry—confidence in your ability to be okay. Even small steps like this build strength over time. Would you like to check in again in a few days, just to see how that peace feels?
2026-03-02 22:41:06,079 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I think that would be great. Thank you again.
2026-03-02 22:41:06,112 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 1 times.
2026-03-02 22:41:06,735 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: You're very welcome. It's meaningful that you're choosing to keep going, even with small steps. I'm glad I could support you. Looking forward to hearing how you're doing in a few days. Take care.
2026-03-02 22:41:08,672 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: You too. Thank you again. Goodbye.
2026-03-02 22:41:08,705 - src.doctor - INFO - Doctor has detected end of conversation 2 times.
2026-03-02 22:41:09,329 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for being so open and honest—your willingness to reflect is already a strength. I’ll be here whenever you’re ready to talk again. Take care, and I hope your day continues to feel grounded and kind.
