2026-03-02 22:47:55,805 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor greeting: Hello, how are you feeling today? Any concerns or feelings you'd like to share? I'm here to listen and help with whatever you're going through.
2026-03-02 22:48:00,133 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I’ve been trying to process what happened with my boyfriend and my best friend — it’s been hard to even look at the memories without feeling a sharp pain in my chest
2026-03-02 22:48:00,663 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: Thank you for sharing that. It sounds like those memories are still very present and emotionally charged. What would you say is the most painful part of the memory—something specific that stands out?
2026-03-02 22:48:04,944 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I guess it’s the knowledge that he’s still talking to my best friend — she’s going to be at the wedding, and he’s still in contact with her
2026-03-02 22:48:05,362 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: That must feel deeply unfair and hurtful. What do you think that connection reminds you of, in terms of your own feelings about the relationship?
2026-03-02 22:48:08,475 - src.sim - INFO - Patient: I don’t know, it feels like the connection they have is stronger than the one I have with him
2026-03-02 22:48:09,011 - src.sim - INFO - Doctor: It’s understandable to feel that way when your bond feels overshadowed. What would it mean, in your mind, for you to feel that your relationship with him was truly valued or seen?
