2026-03-02 23:01:11,724 - src.sim - INFO - Expanded patient history: Over the past week, I’ve been going through a lot of emotional turmoil, especially around my relationship with my boyfriend. We’ve been together for over five years, and I always thought we were building something solid—something that would eventually lead to a commitment, maybe even an engagement. I’ve been so focused on planning every detail: when we’d travel, what we’d do on our anniversary, even how we’d decorate the wedding. I believed that if I just stayed organized, everything would fall into place. That sense of control has always been my anchor. When I found out that my best friend had been involved in an affair with my boyfriend—something I didn’t know about until a year ago—I felt like my entire world had collapsed. I couldn’t believe it. I thought, *If this is how he treats me and my closest friend, then everything else is just as flawed.*  

I remember being furious at first—so angry that I felt like I’d been completely deceived. I didn’t just feel betrayed; I felt like I’d been made to live in a lie. I started questioning every decision I’d ever made, every moment I’d spent trusting people. I thought about whether I’d ever really known my boyfriend, or if he was just using me to feel secure. That anger turned into sadness, and then into a deep sense of loneliness. I’ve been avoiding social situations, even calling my best friend to talk, because I don’t know how to face her anymore. I feel like I’ve lost something fundamental—my trust in relationships, in people, and in myself. I keep thinking, *What if I’m not enough for someone to truly care about me?*  

Recently, my boyfriend suggested that my best friend be part of our wedding plans. I was horrified. I couldn’t understand how he could even bring that up. I felt like I was being asked to celebrate something that had already broken me. I told him I didn’t see how that could work, and I’ve since been replaying that conversation in my head. I don’t trust that he’s being sincere anymore. It makes me feel like I’m walking through a maze where every turn reveals a new betrayal. I’m not sure if I can keep going with this relationship. I’ve been thinking about it a lot, and honestly, it’s hard to imagine a future where I feel safe, seen, or truly loved.  

I’ve also been thinking about another man—someone who’s been interested in me for a year now. I don’t know why I didn’t see it before. I’ve never really considered a relationship outside of my current one, not because I don’t like him, but because I’ve always believed that I need to be in control. If I let myself open up to someone new, I feel like I might lose that structure. But lately, I’ve been scared—scared of being alone, scared of not being loved, and scared that I might be unlovable. I don’t know if I’m making the right choice, but I can’t keep pretending that everything is fine. I just want to feel safe again, and I don’t know how to do that when I feel so untrusted, so broken.
