2026-03-02 23:07:38,197 - src.sim - INFO - Expanded patient history: Over the past week, I’ve been going through a lot of emotional turmoil, especially around my relationship with my boyfriend. We’ve been together for nearly five years, and we were actually planning to get engaged soon—something I had spent so much time preparing for, down to the exact date, the venue, and even the ring. I always thought that if I stayed true to my plans, everything would go right. That’s why I’ve always kept such strict structure in my life—every day, every decision, every moment. It’s like having a roadmap so I don’t feel lost. But now, everything feels like it’s off course.  

It all started when I found out my boyfriend had been in an affair with my best friend. I didn’t know about it at first—she was always so close to him, and I trusted her completely. When I finally found out, it shattered me. I felt completely betrayed, like someone had taken something sacred from me. I thought, *If he could do this to me, how can I trust anything else?* I couldn’t believe it was possible, especially after all the time I’d spent building this relationship with intention. That moment made me question everything—my trust, my decisions, even whether I was truly worthy of love.  

Since then, I’ve been trying to hold on to some sense of control, which is why I’ve been planning everything—what to say to my boyfriend, how to respond to his recent proposal that includes my best friend as a bridesmaid. I can’t even begin to process how strange that feels. The idea of her being part of our wedding makes me feel like I’m being used or manipulated. I keep thinking, *Is he really committed to me, or is this just another way to show off his connections?* It makes me feel suspicious, and I can’t shake the thought that he might have done this before, or that I’ve been blind to the truth all along.  

Lately, I’ve been thinking about another man who’s been interested in me for about a year. I never thought about it before because I believed I had to stay with the person I was committed to. But now, with everything falling apart, I find myself wondering if I wasted years on someone who wasn’t truly loyal. I’m scared—scared of making the wrong choice, scared of being alone again, and scared of not being enough. I don’t know if I should walk away from my boyfriend or if I should give this other man a chance. I keep coming back to the idea that maybe I’m not good enough to be loved in a real, honest way. It’s overwhelming, and I just want someone to see me clearly—not just as someone who follows plans, but as someone who deserves to be loved.
